Subject: [PATCH] drm/ttm: fix swapped-out resources never leaving their bulk_move range

Backport the net effect of the upstream fix and its application correction:
  https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/drm/misc/kernel/-/commit/3db7d7d583419f7b1f2e141e36418802dbb25cf8
  https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/drm/misc/kernel/-/commit/fcfe64715b425262af1b36f498f9197f3537ceed

Upstream author: Vadim Nikitushkin <bub4z0r@gmail.com>
Bug: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/drm/amd/-/issues/5387

The first commit accidentally changed the ttm_resource_try_charge() error
check in ttm_bo_alloc_at_place(). The follow-up restores that check and
changes the intended condition after ttm_tt_swapout(). Linux 7.2.2 has
neither that allocation refactor nor the accidental change, so only the
swapout hunk is needed here.

ttm_tt_swapout() returns a positive page count on successful nonempty
swapout, not zero. Remove the now-unevictable resource from its bulk_move
range on success, avoiding dangling range endpoints when it is later freed.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/ttm/ttm_bo.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/ttm/ttm_bo.c
@@ -1178,7 +1178,7 @@
 
 	if (ttm_tt_is_populated(tt)) {
 		ret = ttm_tt_swapout(bdev, tt, swapout_walk->gfp_flags);
-		if (!ret) {
+		if (ret > 0) {
 			spin_lock(&bdev->lru_lock);
 			ttm_resource_del_bulk_move_unevictable(bo->resource, bo);
 			ttm_resource_move_to_lru_tail(bo->resource);
